            <ArticleTitle>Leiomyoma of the urinary bladder: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>432-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1590/S1677-5538.IBJU.2013.03.18</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case of a 71-year-old woman who presented with one year history of pelvic pain and occasional dysuria is reported. Computed tomography and Magnetic Resonance Imaging revealed a well defined intramural bladder mass. The histological findings of the surgical specimen confirmed a leiomyoma of the urinary bladder. The clinical presentation,imaging findings and management of this relatively rare benign tumor are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
